    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0476" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg394"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[With one enclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Bigelow to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 117.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            Paris</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-04">June 13,
                            1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> A statement of the minister secretary of
                    state a few days since in the corps legislatif, and an article in the Moniteur
                    of the 10th instant, have compelled me to break the silence I intended to have
                    kept until I heard from you in reference to the grounds upon which the minister
                    of foreign affairs placed his withdrawal of the proclamation of neutrality of
                    June, 1865. I transmit herewith a copy of a note which I addressed this morning
                    to his excellency the minister of foreign affairs, which will sufficiently
                    explain itself, and my motives for not permitting the ministerial statements
                    cited in it to pass in silence.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN BIGELOW.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hon. William H. Seward,</hi> Secretary of
                        State.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d371-a1.xml" xpointer="d371-a1"/>
